{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/733178-indefinite-gauru-form-and-new-wolf-gift","id":733178,"title":"Indefinite Gauru form (and new Wolf Gift)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-27T15:16:25-07:00","id":733178,"title":"Indefinite Gauru form (and new Wolf Gift)","content":"In my home games I like to mix in a little Apocalypse with my Forsaken. One of the things I've always had ported over is Limitless Gauru Form. Now, on how to do that is the question. My proposed hack is to disable the healing factor unless in Wasu-im or Basu-im, unless a Uratha falls below a certain health limit (1/2 health, first Wound penalty?) and then they roll Resolve + Composure or instantly enter Wasu-Im and heal that whole bit. A success allows them to spend Essence and hopefully heal up above the limit. Making Combat a struggle to stay out of rage while in the Warform, but something manageable.<br /> <br /> I'd cause Lunacy like Urshul, and I would keep the minus to Defense though, making it, truly, the killing form. However Down and Dirty and uber-Regeneration become a product of Rage. A Werewolf can surrender to Rage and Enter Basu-Im while in Gauru form, and use rules per vanilla WtF basically.<br /> <br /> As for the new Purity gift? I'd bring back Primordial Form. It uses the same rules as Gauru form in base WtF, and perhaps a +1 to Strength, Stamina, and Size with maybe 1/1 Armor. Whenever you Go into Kuruth roll Purity, on a success you enter Primordial Form. I'd also have it count as Gauru form for purposes of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-27-2015, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T00:10:47-07:00","id":734029,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Here's the new Gauru stat block.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GAURU</b><br /> Gauru is the classic wolfman of legend. Enormous, fearsome, and devastating, Gauru Uratha weigh almost four times their Hishu counterparts. While bipedal, they stand one and a half times their Hishu height. They\u2019re bulky, with arms the size of most people\u2019s waists, legs like tree trunks, and teeth like chef\u2019s knives. When a shapeshifter assumes this form, it shows that the time for negotiations is over. The Uratha inflict Lunacy when wearing their battle-form. Even though Uratha in Gauru form can speak, the Rage usually forces the werewolf to kill. When a Uratha takes more than half their Health levels in Lethal damage (rounded down) the Rage takes over and they must roll Resolve + Composure to remain in control, if the roll fails the Uratha immediately falls into Wasu-Im After that point, she must choose: Shift down into Dalu or Urshul, or fall into Kuruth. If she does not shift, roll Resolve + Composure as a reflexive action. If she succeeds, she has one more turn in Gauru, then must shift to Dalu or Urshul, and enters Wasu-Im. If she fails, she enters Basu-Im immediately. <br /> <br /> \u2022<b> Regeneration:</b> Uratha in Gauru form regenerate damage as in other forms, if they fall into Wasu-Im or Basu-Im they regenerate all Lethal or Bashing damage every turn while they are still in Rage. \u2022 <b>Lunacy:</b> Sight of the Gauru form inflicts Lunacy (see p.101). When in Rage onlookers suffer a -2 to Lunacy rolls.<br /> \u2022 <b>Rage:</b> After a Uratha falls into Rage the Gauru-form Uratha must attack an active opponent within striking range each turn. She does not have to continue to attack a crippled opponent as long as another opponent exists. If an opponent is out of reach, she can move toward or throw things at opponent. If she has no opponents, she will attack anything she can reach. If she does anything else, roll Resolve + Composure or fall into Kuruth. A Uratha can voluntarily choose to give into Rage if they are in Gauru form, doing this activates all abilities that come with Rage.<br /> \u2022 <b>Primal Fear:</b> In normal combat, opponents count only their Dexterity or Wits to their Defense; they may not add the appropriate Skill (normally Athletics). If a Gauru-form werewolf falls into Rage it forces all lesser enemies \u2014 including most humans, spirits of lower Rank, and non-supernatural animals \u2014 to use Down and Dirty combat (see p. 165). If the prey hides in a group of more powerful enemies, resolve the combat as normal.<br /> --------------<br /> Anything not mentioned here is the same as WtF, that's all the changed things. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T00:21:51-07:00","id":734042,"title":"","content":"My primary thought is that I have no idea whether your mention of a &quot;new Purity Gift&quot; is meant to imply that this is supposed to be distinct from simply giving everybody The Father's Form for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T00:34:27-07:00","id":734059,"title":"","content":"Well, I haven't finished the new Gift. It'll be a redux of Primal Form, I think. <br /> <br /> As for the difference between the hack and Father's Form. It comes down to the ability to fight in Gauru without immediately entering <i>Kuruth</i>. One rather simple fact. It really comes down to a new Trigger for Death Rage while in Gauru. I also feel like just giving everyone Father's Form takes away from Purity focused Werewolves, and just eliminates one Gift. Now if there's any suggestions for a new Purity Wolf Gift, I am open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T01:30:02-07:00","id":734092,"title":"","content":"Crazy idea: flip normal Gauru and Father's Form.<br /> <br /> Normally, Uratha who enter Gauru are using the dialled down version you get with Father's Form, and they can only get the beefy, beefy version while in Wasu-Im or Basu-Im. However, Father's Form lets you ever-so-briefly control the unrestrained might of Papa Wolf's rage.<br /> <br /> In other words, Father's Form dials up Lunacy and gives you Rage, but also gives you all the Regeneration and let's you leave Gauru without suffering a Breaking Point towards Flesh.<br /> <br /> It's <i>basically</i> the same as your hack, except it keeps that poorly restrained RAGE feel we all love so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:49:39-07:00","id":735050,"title":"","content":"I actually like that a lot. I would have to make it where an Uratha in Gauru cannot choose to fall to Rage, but with the Facet they can. Which brings up something else. What happens when a Uratha shifts out of Gauru after going Wasu-Im? My gut feeling is to say Rage resets after every scene, so if you fall into Rage you either back down and go Dalu, and lose the ability to go Gauru without falling to Basu-Im.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:12:40-07:00","id":735121,"title":"","content":"<b>THE FATHER\u2019S FORM (PURITY)</b><br /> With this gift the Rage of the Wolf is harnessed, ever so briefly bringing the Uratha closer to Wolf, but the you can never hold back the Rage indefinitely.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> The Uratha can enter Rage in Gauru form without immediately losing control. When a Uratha falls into Wasu-Im in Gauru form she has Stamina + Primal Urge turns in Rage without falling into Wasu-Im. At then end of their Stamina + Primal Urge turns she can choose to shift down from Gauru, and bypass the curse of Rage for a little while.<br /> <br /> I think that about sums it up?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}